# Git Push Skip List

These local repos point at **upstream remotes you do not own**. **Never `git push`** them (including bulk "commit all repos" workflows). Local commits are fine; publishing requires a `jssturm` fork remote.

Canonical list: `.cursor/repos/push-skip-list.json`

| Local path | Upstream remote | Why skip |
|------------|-----------------|----------|
| `zoo-flow` | `Fernado03/zoo-flow` | No write access |
| `agenttrace-luo` | `luoyuctl/agenttrace` | No write access |
| `bernstein` | `sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein` | No write access |
| `omniroute` | `diegosouzapw/OmniRoute` | No write access |

## Agent obligations

1. **Bulk push/commit-to-GitHub** — exclude these four paths always.
2. **Single-repo push** — if user asks to push one of these, explain upstream has no write access; offer fork remote setup instead.
3. **Do not rebase/pull-and-push** upstream branches here unless user explicitly requests sync from upstream (read-only).
